From 167536c20d077fa3eda18b57395d7e62c5bd19e2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Abdelhafid DJIDEL <266947999+hafid-logic@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 21:29:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] tests(kernel-views): pin SysFs list_devices output-capacity
 truncation

### What
Pins `SysFs::list_devices`: the returned count is the number of devices actually copied (min of output capacity and device count), a smaller output is truncated with the prefix preserved, a larger output leaves the tail untouched, and an empty output yields 0.

### Why it matters
The projection must report copied entries, not the total. The existing tests read fixed sysfs leaves but never exercise `list_devices` capacity, so returning the full device count or dropping the capacity clamp survives the suite.

### Mutation evidence (fail-then-pass)
| Mutant | Existing suite | New test |
|---|---|---|
| return `devices.len()` instead of copied `count` | PASS (survives) | FAIL (killed) |
| `count = output.len()` (drop the `min` clamp) | PASS (survives) | FAIL (killed) |

Baseline (clean tree + new test): PASS. Reproduce: `cargo test -p ginux-kernel-views --lib sysfs_list_devices`.

Prepared with AI assistance; reviewed by me.
---
 crates/ginux-kernel-views/src/lib.rs | 46 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 46 insertions(+)

diff --git a/crates/ginux-kernel-views/src/lib.rs b/crates/ginux-kernel-views/src/lib.rs
index 37eb6517..08d12fd7 100644
--- a/crates/ginux-kernel-views/src/lib.rs
+++ b/crates/ginux-kernel-views/src/lib.rs
@@ -691,4 +691,50 @@ mod tests {
             Err(ViewError::ReadOnly)
         );
     }
+
+    #[test]
+    fn sysfs_list_devices_truncates_to_output_capacity() {
+        let devices = [
+            DeviceView {
+                name: DeviceName::new(b"null").unwrap(),
+                kind: DeviceKind::Null,
+                major: 1,
+                minor: 3,
+            },
+            DeviceView {
+                name: DeviceName::new(b"zero").unwrap(),
+                kind: DeviceKind::Zero,
+                major: 1,
+                minor: 5,
+            },
+            DeviceView {
+                name: DeviceName::new(b"random").unwrap(),
+                kind: DeviceKind::Random,
+                major: 1,
+                minor: 8,
+            },
+        ];
+        let sys = SysFs::new(&devices, 2);
+        let pad = DeviceView {
+            name: DeviceName::new(b"pad").unwrap(),
+            kind: DeviceKind::Null,
+            major: 0,
+            minor: 0,
+        };
+        // smaller output: truncated, prefix preserved
+        let mut small = [pad; 2];
+        assert_eq!(sys.list_devices(&mut small), 2);
+        assert_eq!(small[0].name.as_bytes(), b"null");
+        assert_eq!(small[1].name.as_bytes(), b"zero");
+        // exact fit
+        let mut exact = [pad; 3];
+        assert_eq!(sys.list_devices(&mut exact), 3);
+        assert_eq!(exact[2].name.as_bytes(), b"random");
+        // larger output: untouched tail
+        let mut big = [pad; 4];
+        assert_eq!(sys.list_devices(&mut big), 3);
+        assert_eq!(big[3].name.as_bytes(), b"pad");
+        // empty output
+        assert_eq!(sys.list_devices(&mut []), 0);
+    }
 }
